    {
      "id": "9b8865f3-1130-4312-99cc-1d61359481f6",
      "name": "README - Setup Workflow",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -64,
        -224
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 550,
        "height": 1068,
        "content": "# SETUP WORKFLOW — INSTALLATION GUIDE\n\n## Purpose\nRun this workflow once after importing the product. It prepares the persistent workflow state and verifies the external services used by the main workflow.\n\n## First-run procedure\n1. Open the credential fields on the two test nodes (in the green section to the right).\n2. Select your **Bright Data** and **OpenAI** credentials.\n3. Execute the `Run Setup` node.\n4. Inspect the `Setup Test Summary` node at the end. \n5. If everything passes, activate the main workflow!\n\n## Persistent State (`last_id`)\nThe main workflow runs every minute and uses `last_id` as the cursor to fetch only *new* posts. This setup creates the `workflow_state` Data Table and initializes that cursor to `0`.\n\n **WARNING**: Re-running this setup workflow will reset `last_id` to `0`. If the main workflow has already processed production data, do NOT rerun setup unless you intentionally want to reset the cursor.\n\n## Troubleshooting\n**Bright Data test fails:**\n- Ensure your API token is valid and the `fetch_truths` zone exists.\n- If `Missing zone parameter`, verify the request is POST with `zone` in the JSON body.\n\n**ChatGPT test fails:**\n- Check the OpenAI API key.\n- Ensure `gpt-4o-mini` is accessible to the account.\n\n## Security\nNever store API keys in Data Tables, Set nodes, or sticky notes. Use n8n credentials for all secrets!"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "08a5884d-6ad0-47f6-b04c-df74c3fae005",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
